vendor/compression is seven libraries compiled into one. Each keeps its own licence, reproduced
below in full from the pinned source archives (pkg/vendor/compression/fetch.toml). All are
permissive and allow static and dynamic linking.

A PROGRAM THAT SHIPS THIS LIBRARY -- linked statically into it, or compression.dll /
compression_<os>_<arch>.so beside it -- must carry the notices the BSD-style licences below
require -- zstd's and lz4's (binary redistributions reproduce the notice), brotli's (in all
copies), and minizip's Info-ZIP part (in the documentation; this library is not an Info-ZIP
release and must not be presented as one) -- and this file, shipped with the program or its
documentation, does it. zlib's, liblzma's (0BSD) and bzip2's licences ask nothing of a binary.

  zlib 1.4 ............ zlib licence
  minizip (zlib 1.4) .. zlib licence; its crypt.h (PKWARE traditional encryption) Info-ZIP licence
  zstd 1.6.0 .......... BSD 3-Clause (zstd is dual-licensed BSD / GPLv2; the BSD licence is taken)
  liblzma (xz 5.8.4) .. BSD Zero Clause (0BSD); xz's tools, not built here, are licensed apart
  brotli 1.2.1 ........ MIT
  lz4 1.11.1 .......... BSD 2-Clause (the library; lz4's command-line tool, GPLv2, is not built)
  bzip2 1.0.8 ......... bzip2 licence (BSD-style)

